<!-- @after Common Pitfalls :: check -->
### Try the decision

<details><summary>Ktor uses the OkHttp engine. Has every transport behaviour changed?</summary>

No. The client API changed while OkHttp remains the engine. Inventory configuration, plugin interactions and defaults instead of treating the library name as the transport contract.
</details>

<details><summary>MockEngine passes. What remains untested?</summary>

The selected real engine’s sockets, TLS, proxies, connection reuse and integration with platform networking. Use appropriate transport integration tests as well as portable contract tests.
</details>

<details><summary>What result would justify keeping Retrofit?</summary>

If its supported platform scope and operational behaviour meet the product’s needs, a migration must show enough value to outweigh compatibility, training and rollout costs. There is no requirement to replace a working boundary.
</details>
